# Everything is versioned. The only exception is a SECRET.
#
# Rationale (EOP ADR-086, adopted fleet-wide): a directory that holds an open
# question or a verdict is memory, not execution — keeping it out of git has
# already caused real loss. Diff noise (counters, timestamps) is a
# commit-granularity decision, not a reason to ignore a file.
#
# `.claude/` and `.continue/` are versioned ON PURPOSE. Do not add them here.
# Any new exception beyond secrets requires an ADR in docs/decisions.md, never
# a silent line in this file.

# Secrets and credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p8
*.p12
*.pfx

# Local agent overrides (may contain machine-specific paths and tokens)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Build output — derived, reproducible, and never memory. The exception is
# written down in docs/decisions.md as ADR-011, because this file says a new
# exception beyond secrets requires one.
target/
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
apps/notes-app/src-tauri/gen/schemas/

# Generated test corpus — tools/gen-large.sh rebuilds it deterministically (ADR-011)
fixtures/large/
fixtures/deep/

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The AUR package's source, copied in by `gen-pkgbuild.sh` for a local build,
# and the PKGBUILD it generates. Both come from `PKGBUILD.in` and version.md.
packaging/aur/notes-bin/PKGBUILD
packaging/aur/notes-bin/*.tar.gz
dist-release/

# Per-machine signing credentials — a secret, which is the one thing this file
# is allowed to exclude. The keychain is the preferred home for both the
# Developer ID and the notarisation password (ADR-070); this is the escape hatch
# for a machine that needs an override, and `~/.config/tura-notes/build.env` is
# the same file kept outside the tree entirely.
signing.env
